 ```
 
+##### limit
+
+The maximum number of subranges to return from one header, defaults to no
+limit. When the header has more subranges than `limit` (counted after
+`combine`, if enabled, and ignoring invalid or unsatisfiable ranges), they are
+merged into a single subrange from the lowest start to the highest end. Bytes
+between the original subranges are included in the result.
+
+<!-- eslint-disable no-undef -->
+
+```js
+parseRange(1000, 'bytes=500-600,0-10,20-30', { limit: 2 })
+// => [
+//      { start: 0, end: 600 }
+//    ]
+```
+
